Summary of verified identities and structural facts: 
 [Generalized, swept over n = 3 to 12 ] 
  * Interior angle theta = (n-2) pi / n 
  * Exterior angle = central angle = 2 pi / n 
  * Flat-vertex count k_flat = floor(2 pi / theta) 
  * Loop-closure index k_loop = 2n / gcd(2n, n-2) 
  * R(2 pi/n)^n = I; det R = 1; tr R = 2 cos(2 pi / n) 
  * R^k traces matched 2 cos(2 pi k/n) for k = 1..n 
  * Primary basis vectors v[k] = (cos, sin)(pi/2 + 2 pi k/n) 
  * Edge vectors e[k] computed and reported 
  * Side length s = 2 sin(pi/n) (unit circumradius) 
  * Z_n holonomy: order(g) = n/gcd(g,n) 
  * Z_2 (spinor) and Z_n (anyonic) cases both verified 
  * Alexander-Orbach: d_spec = 2 d_eff / d_w (n-independent) 
  * charpoly(C_n) divides x^n - 1; C_n is orthogonal 
  * Real-invariant 2D subspaces V_k of C_n enumerated 
  * Projectors P_diag, P_perp idempotent, orthogonal, complete 
  * dim(E_perp) = n - 2 (after taking V_1 as physical plane) 
  * Outer-totalistic n-neighbor binary rule count = 2^(2(n+1)) 
  * Diagonals d[k] = sin(k pi/n)/sin(pi/n) 
  * Area A = (n/4) cot(pi/n) 
  * Dihedral D_n: |D_n| = 2n, S R S = R^{-1} 
  * D_n irrep dim^2 sum = 2n (case n even / n odd) 
  * Star K_{1,n} Laplacian spectrum = {0, 1 x n, n+1} 
  * Cycle C_n Laplacian eigenvalues = 2 - 2 cos(2 pi k/n) 
 [Pentagon-specific benchmarks verified] 
  * phi^2 = phi + 1; phi*(phi-1) = 1; 1/phi = phi - 1 
  * Fibonacci recursion phi^n = F_n phi + F_{n-1} 
  * Binet formula F_n = (phi^n - psi^n)/sqrt(5) 
  * Pentagon diagonal/side = phi 
  * Pentagram self-similarity: 1/phi^2 = 2 - phi 
  * Z[phi] arithmetic, N(phi^n) = (-1)^n 
